This is a miscompilation bug in SeparateConstOffsetFromGEP.
Issue title: separate-const-offset-from-gep miscompile related to "trunc nuw"
Detailed information:
BUG TYPE:
    miscompilation

VERIFICATION RESULT:
    Invalid refinement in @pr154116_nsw -- Target is more poisonous than source

VIOLATED PROPERTY:
    poison refinement

SOURCE (pre-transformation IR):
target triple = "x86_64-unknown-unknown"
define ptr @pr154116_nsw(ptr %p, i128 %i) {
  %idx = add i128 %i, 1
  %idx.conv = trunc nsw i128 %idx to i64
  %arrayidx = getelementptr i32, ptr %p, i64 %idx.conv
  ret ptr %arrayidx
}

TARGET (post-transformation IR):
target triple = "x86_64-unknown-unknown"
define ptr @pr154116_nsw(ptr %p, i128 %i) {
  %1 = trunc nsw i128 %i to i64
  %2 = getelementptr i32, ptr %p, i64 %1
  %arrayidx2 = getelementptr i8, ptr %2, i64 4
  ret ptr %arrayidx2
}

WHAT THE TRANSFORMATION CHANGED:
  only in target:
    %1: %1 = trunc nsw i128 %i to i64
    %2: %2 = getelementptr i32, ptr %p, i64 %1
    %arrayidx2: %arrayidx2 = getelementptr i8, ptr %2, i64 4
  only in source:
    %idx: %idx = add i128 %i, 1
    %idx.conv: %idx.conv = trunc nsw i128 %idx to i64
    %arrayidx: %arrayidx = getelementptr i32, ptr %p, i64 %idx.conv

CRITICAL VALUES:
    %arrayidx
    %arrayidx2
    %idx
    %idx.conv

DEPENDENCY CHAIN (source):
    %idx = add i128 %i, 1
    %idx.conv = trunc nsw i128 %idx to i64
    %arrayidx = getelementptr i32, ptr %p, i64 %idx.conv

CONTROL FLOW (blocks entered by the failing execution):
    (none)

COUNTEREXAMPLE INPUT:
    ptr %p = pointer(non-local, block_id=0, offset=3) / Address=#x0000000000000003
    i128 %i = #xffffffffffffffff7fffffffffffffff (340282366920938463454151235394913435647, -9223372036854775809)

DIVERGENCE (source vs target on that input):
    %arrayidx2: source = (not computed)   target = poison

MEMORY STATE:
  source:
===================
NON-LOCAL BLOCKS:
Block 0 >	size: 0	align: 1	alloc type: 0	alive: false	address: 0
Block 1 >	size: 0	align: 1	alloc type: 0	alive: true	address: 2

INTERPRETATION:
    A transformation may only make a program *less* poisonous. Wherever the source produces a well-defined value, the target must produce the same value -- it may not produce poison.
    On the input above the source yields pointer(non-local, block_id=0, offset=3) / Address=#x0000000000000003 while the target yields poison.
    The earliest reported divergence is at %arrayidx2.

